    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0259" n="993" xml:id="pg993"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ransom to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                        1895</hi></date>. (Received Sept. 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 69.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit the inclosed
                    copies of a letter from Secretary Mariscal, requesting me to act as arbitrator
                    in the designated convention between Mexico and Guatemala. Copies of a similar,
                    letter from the Guatemalan minister, Mr. Emilio de Leon, have already been sent
                    to your Department.</p>
                <p>I have not felt at liberty to accept this trust without your approbation. I see
                    no chance for any unpleasant complication in anyway with our Government. I
                    should like an answer by telegraph.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">M. W. Ransom.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d176-a1.xml" xpointer="d176-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
